<Blog title="My thoughts on AI">
    <h1>My thoughts on AI</h1>
    <p class="date">Posted on 2026-11-25</p>

    <p>
        In the past couple of years, AI went from "there are 2 Rs in 'strawberry'"
        to becoming a tool that most programmers frequently use to debug or write
        code. It is no doubt that such a change is a substantial one, and that it
        happened in a few short years, during which, lots of people developed
        reliance on their AI models, unable to write a simple for loop on their own 
        anymore.
    </p>
    <p>
        I recently came across a Youtube channel named Hayyoth, and he embraced
        extreme minimalism. He gained a shit ton of subscribers in like a month 
        with a very simple setup. Blank grey desktop, a small Vim window open, 
        and a window named Human with a man emoji that I can't remember from 
        memory. He also had a very satisfying program that plays a crisp keyboard
        press sound when a key is pressed. Its evident why people love him. 
    </p>

